INT. STRANDED CABLE-CAR GONDOLA - DUSK

Wind shrieks. The gondola sways on its cable a thousand feet above a white abyss. Ice rimes the windows. A single emergency bulb flickers.

ELSPETH (60s, mountaineering jacket, calm) braces against the door. TARIQ (30s, ski instructor's red parka) tries to pry open a roof hatch. MIREILLE (40s, silk scarf, bare hands) holds a toddler's mitten and no toddler. GUS "TINY" PAPADAKIS (50s, enormous, wearing a rented jacket two sizes small) sits on the floor with his head between his knees. BEATRIZ (20s, backpack on her lap, headphones around her neck) holds a radio handset.

BEATRIZ
(into handset)
Dispatch, are you there?

RESCUE DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio, crackling)
Gondola Four, we copy. Hold position. Repeat, hold position.

TARIQ
Hold position? We are the position!

Elspeth lays a hand on his arm. He shakes it off, then steps back, ashamed.

ELSPETH
Nobody panics. Not yet.

GUS
(muffled, to his knees)
I'm not panicking. I'm meditating.

The gondola lurches. Everyone grabs a rail. The bulb dies. Beatriz clicks a flashlight on and turns the beam to the ceiling.

MIREILLE
(whisper)
Please. Please.

ELSPETH
(to the group)
Okay. Listen to me. Everyone's watch, everyone's phone, everyone's jacket. We pool it. Now.

They hesitate. Then Gus lifts his head, unzips the tiny jacket, and holds it out. Tariq follows. Mireille hands over her scarf with trembling fingers. Beatriz shares her headphones, her gloves, her granola bar.

RESCUE DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Gondola Four, storm front arrives in forty minutes. Do not exit the cabin.

Tariq looks at the hatch. He looks at the drop. He sits.

TARIQ
(to himself)
Forty minutes. Forty minutes.

Elspeth wraps the scarf around Mireille's neck and presses the mitten into her palm. Mireille grips it. Wind rattles the glass.

BEATRIZ
(into handset)
Dispatch, we'll hold. But please hurry.
